Shelves Loader — NOTICE

Shelves Loader (MIT) is the standalone host for Deck Shelves. It was developed
independently (clean-room): no source code from the projects below was copied,
and no binary or package from them is redistributed.

Acknowledgement of the techniques this loader re-implements from
observable behaviour only:

- plugin loader — https://github.com/SteamDeckHomebrew/a plugin loader (GPL-2.0)
  Reference for the overall standalone-host concept: enabling CEF remote
  debugging, injecting a bundle into the Steam renderer, tracking the renderer
  lifecycle, and adding a Quick Access Menu tab. Behaviour was studied and
  re-implemented from scratch against the public Chrome DevTools Protocol; no
  plugin loader code (GPL-2.0) was copied or adapted — doing so is deliberately
  avoided to keep this project under the MIT license.

- a frontend library / the packages / the packages —
  https://github.com/SteamDeckHomebrew/a frontend library (LGPL-2.1)
  Reference for locating Steam's webpack UI modules and the React-tree patch
  helpers (afterPatch / findInReactTree / fiber refresh) used by the injected
  host runtime. Re-implemented from scratch; the `the packages` packages are never
  bundled.

The Steam client, the Steam UI components located at runtime, and the SteamOS
platform are property of Valve Corporation and are not redistributed here.

See also the shared host runtime's NOTICE (@deck-shelves/host).
